  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Layer rule",
      "items": [
        "lkctl reaches the Management API only through the resource façades",
        "forbidigo in .golangci.yml rejects cmd/ references to Client.APIClient, Client.<X>API, NewAPIClient and *APIService",
        "An operation without a façade gets a façade method in pkg/client first",
        "lkctl still uses managementv1 model types for request bodies and results"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Escape hatch",
      "items": [
        "Client embeds the generated *APIClient, so every generated service is a field on Client",
        "Application code may use it for operations without a façade; lkctl may not",
        "Wrap its errors with client.WrapAPIError to get the façades' error type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Imports not drawn",
      "items": [
        "Umbrella → core and generated SDK (auth sources, model aliases)",
        "lkctl → core, generated models, pkg/common, pkg/version",
        "Client → pkg/version (User-Agent) and apache/iceberg-go (CatalogV1)",
        "Storage helpers → generated models; pkg/permissions imports nothing from this module"
      ]
    }
  ]
